{"abstract":[{"text":"A type that represents a globally-unique actor that can be used to isolate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"various declarations anywhere in the program.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GlobalActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SendableMetatype","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SendableMetatype","preciseIdentifier":"s:s16SendableMetatypeP"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that conforms to the "},{"code":"GlobalActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol and is marked with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"code":"@globalActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute can be used as a custom attribute. Such types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are called global actor types, and can be applied to any declaration to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specify that such types are isolated to that global actor type. When using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such a declaration from another actor (or from nonisolated code),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"synchronization is performed through the shared actor instance to ensure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutually-exclusive access to the declaration."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Custom Actor Executors","anchor":"Custom-Actor-Executors","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A global actor uses a custom executor if it needs to customize its execution"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"semantics, for example, by making sure all of its invocations are run on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specific thread or dispatch queue."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is done the same way as with normal non-global actors, by declaring a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Actor\/unownedExecutor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" nonisolated property in the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/GlobalActor\/ActorType","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"underlying this global actor."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" necessary to override the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/GlobalActor\/sharedUnownedExecutor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" static"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property of the global actor, as its default implementation already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delegates to the "},{"code":"shared.unownedExecutor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is the most reasonable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and correct implementation of this protocol requirement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can find out more about custom executors, by referring to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol’s documentation."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"See Also","type":"aside"